        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: ವನವಾಸ",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ವನವಾಸ — vanavāsa — \"exile in the forest\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಕಥೆಯಲ್ಲಿ ರಾಜಕುಮಾರ ಹನ್ನೆರಡು ವರ್ಷ ವನವಾಸ ಮಾಡಿದನು. katheyalli rājakumāra hanneraḍu varṣa vanavāsa māḍidanu. In the story the prince spent twelve years in exile in the forest."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The epics are full of ವನವಾಸ (vanavāsa); today it can mean any long hard time away."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ವನವಾಸ (vanavāsa) is borrowed from Sanskrit vanavāsa, \"dwelling in the forest\" (CDIAL 11265a), from vana \"forest\" and vāsa \"dwelling\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for telling what happened."
            }
          ]
